From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0335-frizti-05-macro-state-writes-through-the-sink.patch

Source: 0335-frizti-05-macro-state-writes-through-the-sink.patch
maxwell_3d: macro state writes go through the back's method sink (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone, and before or after lichii-gpu 0214.

Source: Frizti/Lichii 516ba08ce5 and 4ddc1a058d (Dr. Sergio, Lichii PR 166), 3D part,
GPL-3.0-or-later. Frizti's v2 build keeps it opt-in.

EDEN_NX2_MACRO_SINK=1. A macro's state write costs the back a full CallMethod. The command list's own
state writes only go in the method sink, applied in one loop before the next executable write. With
the switch macro writes do the same. Order against draws stays: the sink is applied before any
executable or direct write and in FinishFrontMacro. On the back, CallMethod does for such a register
what ConsumeSinkImpl does: shadow RAM, same-value skip, dirty flags.

The split verify check counts sunk writes as done for the shadow RAM too, or it would move the front's
shadow back. EDEN_NX2_3D_METHODS and EDEN_NX2_3D_HISTORY stop seeing these writes: they sit in
CallMethod.

Changed from the source: no ring pairs, no compute part (frizti-04), no counters.

Runs on the PS5: yes. Worth trying only if lichii-gpu-0210 shows the back as the limit.
Hang: no wait added. Pool memory: none beyond the sink vector, which already exists.
Checked: PS5-target syntax compile, alone and on the stack. Not run.

diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp
index e92235d451..c38689a1d5 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/maxwell_3d.cpp
@@ -892,6 +892,19 @@ bool FrontHandledOutsideDrawManager(u32 method) {
     }
 }
 
+// EDEN_NX2_MACRO_SINK=1: a macro's state write goes to the back's method sink, as the command list's
+// own state writes do, instead of a CallMethod each. The back applies the sink in order before the
+// next executable or direct write and in FinishFrontMacro, so the order against draws stays.
+// From Frizti/Lichii 516ba08ce5 and 4ddc1a058d (Dr. Sergio, Lichii PR 166), 3D part. Read at first
+// use: env.txt is applied in main, after the globals (Frizti 5c173ca274).
+bool FrontMacroSink() {
+    static const bool sink = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_MACRO_SINK");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return sink;
+}
+
 // EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_SKIP=0: send state writes that keep the register's value too.
 bool FrontSkipSame() {
     static const bool skip = [] {
@@ -990,7 +1003,7 @@ void Maxwell3D::FrontWrite(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split, FrontState& fs, u32 met
             break;
         }
     }
-    if (from_macro) {
+    if (from_macro && (execution_mask[method] || !FrontMacroSink())) {
         split.MacroWrite(this, method, argument);
     } else {
         split.Method(this, method, argument, is_last_call, nullptr);
@@ -1197,9 +1210,20 @@ void Maxwell3D::FrontVerify(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split, FrontState& fs) {
                                ? shadow_state.reg_array[method]
                                : value;
     }
+    // With EDEN_NX2_MACRO_SINK a tracked macro write reaches the shadow RAM only when the sink is
+    // applied: it counts as done here too, or the check would put the front's shadow back.
+    std::array<u32, Regs::NUM_REGS> expected_shadow;
+    std::memcpy(expected_shadow.data(), shadow_state.reg_array.data(), sizeof(expected_shadow));
+    if (FrontMacroSink() &&
+        (shadow_state.shadow_ram_control == Regs::ShadowRamControl::Track ||
+         shadow_state.shadow_ram_control == Regs::ShadowRamControl::TrackWithFilter)) {
+        for (const auto& [method, value] : method_sink) {
+            expected_shadow[method] = value;
+        }
+    }
     static u64 control_differences{};
     if ((fs.control != shadow_state.shadow_ram_control ||
-         fs.shadow[MAXWELL3D_REG_INDEX(shadow_ram_control)] != shadow_state.reg_array[MAXWELL3D_REG_INDEX(shadow_ram_control)] ||
+         fs.shadow[MAXWELL3D_REG_INDEX(shadow_ram_control)] != expected_shadow[MAXWELL3D_REG_INDEX(shadow_ram_control)] ||
          fs.regs[MAXWELL3D_REG_INDEX(shadow_ram_control)] != expected[MAXWELL3D_REG_INDEX(shadow_ram_control)]) &&
         control_differences < 4) {
         LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU, "Split shadow RAM control writes, front ({} total) / back ({} total):",
@@ -1229,12 +1253,12 @@ void Maxwell3D::FrontVerify(VideoCommon::GpuSplit& split, FrontState& fs) {
         fs.control = shadow_state.shadow_ram_control;
     }
     for (u32 i = 0; i < Regs::NUM_REGS; ++i) {
-        if (fs.shadow[i] != shadow_state.reg_array[i]) {
+        if (fs.shadow[i] != expected_shadow[i]) {
             if (control_differences++ < 16) {
                 LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU, "Split front shadow register {:#x}: front {:#x}, back {:#x}", i,
-                            fs.shadow[i], shadow_state.reg_array[i]);
+                            fs.shadow[i], expected_shadow[i]);
             }
-            fs.shadow[i] = shadow_state.reg_array[i];
+            fs.shadow[i] = expected_shadow[i];
         }
     }
     if ((checks & 63) == 1) {
